Architecture: arm64
Section: libs
Description: QTEE minkteec shared library
 MinkIPC is Qualcomm’s lightweight capability-based inter-process communication (IPC) framework.
 It enables secure, synchronous message passing across different security domains—like Linux
 user space to Trusted Execution Environment—using unforgeable object references and transport
 mechanisms such as SMC, sockets, or TEE IOCTLs.
 .
 This package consists of the shared library libminkteec.
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, ${shlibs:Depends}

Package: libminkipc-dev
Architecture: arm64
Section: libdevel
Description: QTEE shared libraries - devlopment files
 MinkIPC is Qualcomm’s lightweight capability-based inter-process communication (IPC) framework.
 It enables secure, synchronous message passing across different security domains—like Linux
 user space to Trusted Execution Environment—using unforgeable object references and transport
 mechanisms such as SMC, sockets, or TEE IOCTLs.
 .
 This package contains library headers and symlinks for the shared libraries shipped in the
 libminkadaptor0 and libminkteec1 packages.
Depends: libminkadaptor0 (= ${binary:Version}), libminkteec1 (= ${binary:Version}), ${misc:Depends}

Package: minkipc-qteesupplicant
Architecture: arm64
Description: QTEE supplicant - support daemons and udev rules
 MinkIPC is Qualcomm’s lightweight capability-based inter-process communication (IPC) framework.
 It enables secure, synchronous message passing across different security domains—like Linux
 user space to Trusted Execution Environment—using unforgeable object references and transport
 mechanisms such as SMC, sockets, or TEE IOCTLs.
 .
 This package consists of the qteesupplicant and sfsconfig systemd services along with
 its necessary shared library internal to qteesupplicant. It includes udev rules as well
 for qteesupplicant to access QTEE.
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, ${shlibs:Depends}
